`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["When a CA is reissued and the signer is the superseded CA certificate, the VA moves the signer to the new certificate — provided it carries ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"cRLSign"})," — and republishes the CRL. If the new certificate lacks ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"cRLSign"}),", the VA keeps the previous signer and logs a warning. If the signer is any other certificate with the CA’s subject and key, it is deliberately left unchanged; the previous certificate then cannot be deleted while the settings use it (the API returns ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"409"})," ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"certificate is in use"}),"), and to retire it you update the signer with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"PUT"}),"."]}),`
